        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(github-copilot): add native web search for Copilot GPT models",
        "body": "Closes #78573\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nGitHub Copilot GPT/Responses models support hosted web search, but OpenClaw only exposes the managed `web_search` path for this provider. Users therefore need another search provider or get failed/stale results even though their Copilot subscription already includes search.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe GitHub Copilot plugin now replaces the managed function with Copilot's native Responses `web_search` tool when search is enabled and no managed provider is pinned. It is limited to OpenAI-family Copilot models and respects `nativeWebSearchAllowedByToolPolicy`, so `web_search` and `group:web` denies still apply.\n\nDirect OpenAI behavior, auth, core orchestration, and config schemas are unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCopilot Responses users get zero-config hosted search. They can keep managed search by selecting a provider such as `brave`, or disable search with `tools.web.search.enabled: false`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head `54865ec11f` was verified without starting an OpenClaw service:\n\n- The real provider wrapper emitted native `web_search` with `reasoning.effort: \"low\"` for the allowed path. Policy deny, a pinned managed provider, and the internal `goldeneye` alias all kept the managed tool unchanged.\n- Focused tests passed: 4 files, 194 tests.\n- Extension production/test type checks, extension lint, both import-boundary checks, docs formatting/lint, `git diff --check`, and the full build passed.\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  extensions/github-copilot/native-web-search.test.ts \\\n  extensions/github-copilot/stream.test.ts \\\n  src/agents/embedded-agent-runner-extraparams.test.ts \\\n  src/llm/providers/stream-wrappers/openai.test.ts\n```\n\nPrior live proof from May 7, 2026 is retained as backend capability evidence: a direct Copilot `/v1/responses` request returned a completed `web_search_call` with `url_citation`, and an OpenClaw `github-copilot/gpt-5.4` subagent with no managed provider returned current results with citations and no managed-search failure.\n\nThe refreshed head was intentionally not rerun through a local Gateway. Its payload wiring and policy behavior are covered by the current-head probe and tests above; final citation rendering was not retested.\n",
